[
    {
        "content": "<p>Is it possible to quote a <code>stx : Syntax</code> term in such a way that</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval!</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">show</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TermElabM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">7</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">quotedStxTerm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stx</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">elabTerm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">quotedStxTerm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Syntax</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">dbg_trace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>would yield an <code>Expr</code> whose type is <code>Syntax</code> instead of <code>Nat</code>?</p>\n<p>EDIT: It seems Mathlib's <code>ToExpr</code> instance for <code>Syntax</code> can be used for this purpose</p>",
        "id": 579564593,
        "sender_full_name": "nrs",
        "timestamp": 1773597159
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Why do you need this? You could certainly write a <code>Quote Syntax</code> or use something like <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.Elab.Term.quoteAutoTactic#doc\">docs#Lean.Elab.Term.quoteAutoTactic</a> but this seems like something weird to want (unless maybe if you're working with <code>autoParam</code>s)</p>",
        "id": 579565489,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1773598072
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Here is an example usecase: <a href=\"https://github.com/nrs-status/lean_ref/blob/main/metaprogramming/term_elab/examples/writer_monad_let_expansion_stx_version.lean\">https://github.com/nrs-status/lean_ref/blob/main/metaprogramming/term_elab/examples/writer_monad_let_expansion_stx_version.lean</a><br>\nIt's an elaborator that augments a monadic value with a writer wrapper that logs <code>let</code> assignments. I had to simplify the writer's type to avoid dealing with quoting <code>Syntax</code>, but I'd like to be able to keep <code>Syntax</code> information</p>",
        "id": 579565560,
        "sender_full_name": "nrs",
        "timestamp": 1773598145
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>following what mathlib does, the following works:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">deriving</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ToExpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Pos</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Raw</span>\n<span class=\"n\">deriving</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ToExpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Substring</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Raw</span>\n<span class=\"n\">deriving</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ToExpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">SourceInfo</span>\n<span class=\"n\">deriving</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ToExpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Syntax</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 579565958,
        "sender_full_name": "nrs",
        "timestamp": 1773598625
    }
]